  partName: Left Outer Cover (2)
  description: The Left Outer Cover (2) is a large, elongated component situated
    at the middle-left-center of the jet engine, constructed from Outer cover 1 material.
    It plays a crucial role in enclosing and safeguarding the engine's internal components,
    while also contributing to the overall aerodynamic performance of the engine.
    An interesting aspect of this cover is its symmetrical design with the right
    outer cover, allowing for balanced airflow and engine operation.
